    "description": "Polished Lapidary Stone Decorative Accessory\nNatural Polished Stone\n8.0 lbs\nMounted on matching stone base\nThis substantial lapidary piece features a large, polished half-sphere crafted from a natural stone exhibiting rich earth tones, including tan, grey, and deep brown with visible mineral veining. The stone displays a high-gloss finish that highlights its complex geological patterns. It is securely mounted to a rectangular matching stone base, making it an ideal choice for a substantial desktop paperweight, a single bookend, or a decorative shelf accent.\nHalf-sphere design with a flat front face showing the internal stone pattern\nEarth-toned mineral composition with intricate veining and mottling throughout\nRectangular base with felt protective pads on the underside\nSubstantial 8-pound weight provides stability for use as a paperweight or bookend\nApproximately 7 inches height by 7 inches length and 4 inches depth\nCondition:\nVery good condition with a high-polish finish. The stone surfaces are smooth and well-finished. There is a small, shallow chip visible on the outer edge of the circular face, as shown in the detail photos. The base is intact and the mounting is secure. Felt pads on the underside show light wear from previous display.\nPlease Note:\nThis is a pre-owned item being sold\nas-is\n. We do our best to describe items accurately and include research where possible, but we are not experts in every category. Please note that if the title or description states \"Tested\" that we only test to make sure the unit \"\nPOWERS ON\"\n.\nNo further testing takes place unless stated otherwise and items are considered untested.\nPlease remember all items are used and are sold as is, no refunds.If you have questions, please contact us before bidding.\nFor all vintage clothing, please research sizing before placing a bid.\nItems from different time periods may have measurements that differ from today’s standard sizing.\nCustomer Service:\nReach us via the “Contact Us” link above or by calling\n(540) 361-6550\n. Messages are handled Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:00 PM ET, and we strive to respond within 48 hours.",
